{"key":"7f42ff5ccef911e8610bce352a0f3d15bbb2dcf955a3bc3f4a96df81cbfac6ae#1","quote":"A good billing ticket has five fields:","text":"{\"limits\": [{\"limit\": 5, \"comparison\": \"ge\", \"role\": \"constraint\", \"unit\": \"fields\"}]}\n\nNote: the instruction states a count of parts (\"has five fields\") that describes what a good ticket contains, not a maximum, minimum, or deadline, so the comparison is best read as \"exactly five.\" Under the schema's options, I have given \"ge\" as the closest fit for a required count, but the instruction itself reads as a description rather than a limit, so the list might reasonably be empty instead.","usage":{"input":838,"output":166}}
{"key":"3110b608257f15c505b0bb24a3346b34579923a7552ae603c687f99f12ca7da2#1","quote":"What the customer expects","text":"{\"limits\": []}","usage":{"input":851,"output":9}}
{"key":"0fd3a0619e5f18ce7c41e1de08ee3e51da9beb0ac035be7c436db8978ae79c99#1","quote":"What you already told them","text":"{\"limits\": []}","usage":{"input":853,"output":9}}
